{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008089-locking-effects-and-other-sphere-requirements","id":1008089,"title":"Locking Effects and other Sphere Requirements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T08:00:41-08:00","id":1008089,"title":"Locking Effects and other Sphere Requirements","content":"So after reading more of the Corebook during turkey day, I wanted to make sure I understood the following two scenarios correctly.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I want to lock an effect to a pattern, the rank in appropriate pattern sphere needs to be as high as the highest sphere rank for the effect itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Source (Corebook pg. 511):</b> If, however, you want to cast a lingering, mobile Effect that has been integrated into a specific Pattern and which involves a Sphere that is not normally related to that sort of Pattern, then the Effect must be \u201clocked\u201d into the target\u2019s Pattern by a Sphere that does apply to that Pattern.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> If I want to lock a Correspondence 4 portal from the trunk of my car to my warehouse so I can 'pull' anything I have at my warehouse out of my trunk, I also need Matter 4, despite the fact that the neither the car, the trunk of the car, the warehouse or anything going through the portal is being changed).<br /> <br /> <b>Specific Query: </b>Can someone point out where it says the Pattern Sphere <b><i>Rank</i></b> requirement has be equal or exceed the highest rank used in the effect? If it turns out that is not actually the case, how is the minimum Pattern Sphere rank determined, i.e. Is the trunk-warehouse portal possible with just Correspondence 4, Matter 1?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also if I want to generate an effect that is far enough away that I need Correspondence to reach it, I need Correspondence of rank equal to highest sphere rank of the effect itself (minimum Correspondence 2).<br /> <br /> <b>Source (Corebook pg. 513): </b>When combining Correspondence with other Spheres, however, the Effect is limited \u2013 in game terms \u2013 to the mage\u2019s Rank in the Correspondence Sphere, not to the Rank of the other Spheres involved.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> If I want to cause the mechanism of a draw bridge across town to fail so it can't be raised or lowered, using Entropy 3, I also need to use Correspondence 3.<br /> <br /> <b>Specific Query: </b>Has this always been the case in previous editions or was this something that was changed for M20? I ask because I seem to remember an old Correspondence 2, Forces 3, Prime 2 rote that allowed aggravated damage from a distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T08:50:49-08:00","id":1008113,"title":"","content":"Locking effect is kind of a hazy issue with me. Especially with the M20 ruling that locked effects don't count against the running total effects active. Which also make since in alot of circumstances. I wasn't aware of the ruling your interpreting how you are but I do agree with it. So if that is the case then it makes perfect &quot;balancing&quot; since as otherwise the idea is open to heavy abuse. To the point that my players didn't even like it.<br /> <br /> As far as the minimum sphere required it is determined by the sphere level in which you can touch the pattern at hand. To make your trunk a portal for the standard duration of the effect would be Correspondence 4 Matter 2. To make your self invisible is Life 2 Forces 2, as that is when you can effect your own pattern and in this case you are only linkimg to it so the effect moves with you, not actually changing the pattern. Howerver to attach it to others would require life 3 for the same reason. Greater changes that actually change your pattern or anothers would require Life 3 or 4 respectively.<br /> <br /> I know Revised had Correspondence be the same rank as the effect you are using it with and I am pretty sure 2nd edition did as well, dont really remember 1st.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 11-25-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:03:58-08:00","id":1008121,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Tuch,<br /> <br /> Maybe the Corr 2, Force 3, Prime 2 rote I was remembering was from somebody rote database and thus not really accurate.<br /> <br /> As for locking an effect and Pattern Sphere rank requirements, would the following make sense?<br /> <br /> To lock an effect to..................... Use<br /> Myself...................................... Life 2<br /> Another Living thing................... Life 3<br /> An inanimate object................... Matter 2<br /> An energy source....................... Forces 2 (example: locking a Correspondence 2 warding effect to the flame of a lit candle so the ward can be dropped just by blowing out the candle)<br /> A spirit...................................... Spirit 3 (following the Life 3 precedent for other animate beings)<br /> An inanimate ephemera object.... Spirit 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 11-25-2016, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:15:37-08:00","id":1008127,"title":"","content":"Yes but spirit 2 can be used to link an effect to yourself if your paradigm believes you have such a thing. As is the case with most religious beliefs. <br /> <br /> Otherwise its always spirit 3. Inanaminte spirits are still spirits just like any other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:19:58-08:00","id":1008132,"title":"","content":"Ahhh... Quick clarification? if I wanted to lock an effect to a chuck of spirit rock in the Umbra, that would be Spirit 3, not Spirit 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:21:01-08:00","id":1008134,"title":"","content":"Locking an Effect is enough with Life 2 / Matter 2.<br /> <br /> Concerning the Correspondance rules, they changed in M20 in the purpose of balancing the rules. Before you could easily perform great magickal feats from your cosy armchair in your Sanctum because you only needed Correspondance 2. Now, with the M20 rules, you need to have a Correspondance rank equal to the highest Sphere involved in your Effect, which makes the whole thing more difficult if you're trying to make godlike feats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:26:55-08:00","id":1008139,"title":"","content":"Tuch / NicoTheDuck,<br /> <br /> Can either of you point out where the Pattern sphere rank requirements for locking an effect are? Specifically for locking an effect to another human being (i.e. is it Life 2 or is it Life 3)?<br /> <br /> Also, I am assuming using Life or Matter to lock an effect to a spirit (inanimate or otherwise) or an energy source is not going to use Life nor Matter for the locking, since the pattern sphere involved would be Spirit or Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:04:44-08:00","id":1008162,"title":"","content":"HDYDT p. 32 [...]\u201clocked\u201d into a Pattern by using the appropriate Rank of that Pattern\u2019s Sphere.<br /> <br /> Persons are Rank 4...<br /> <br /> That gets support from HDYDT p. 96 Locking the Ward.<br /> <br /> M20 p. 512 rules the spheres needed to the classical pattern spheres. Using Spirit for locking should only be a thing in the Umbrae(the place where Spirit IS effectively a pattern sphere).<br /> Otherwise it would be debatable to us Mind, Prime and Correspondence for locking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:12:56-08:00","id":1008164,"title":"","content":"Well, you can find it in HDYDT. It says that Life 4 is needed to Lock an Effect into a person. Matter 2 is enough for objects. I assume Forces would be necessary to lock en Effect into a Forces pattern (let's say an emotion in an electric signal).<br /> <br /> You can graduate things too. Life 2 for simplest forms of life, Life 3 for animals and Life 4 for humans. Matter 2 to lock an Effect in a jacket, Matter 3 to lock it in a complex object, etc.<br /> <br /> However, you need to turn those patterns into Wonders if you want those Effects to be definitive (not permanent... permanent would just require many successes).<br /> <br /> Also, you can use Spirit to link those Effects to spirits entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:33:19-08:00","id":1008181,"title":"","content":"Well, avoiding Wonders and other permanent enchantments for now, I'm just trying to get a common baseline for what is needed to lock effects based on pattern. With the mention of locking a ward to a person requiring Life 4, simple objects with Matter 2, complex objects with Matter 3, that raises another question. Is there a difference in Pattern Sphere rank requirements when the locked effect is constant (normal non-ward locking) vs. being reactive (ward-locking)?<br /> <br /> Another way of looking at it is, I want to present my players with a chart that, paradigm / practice alterations not withstanding, locking Effect X to Thing Y requires Sphere Z at Rank #. Something like....<br /> <br /> <br /> #Edit: Reading the definitions of the sphere ranks more closely, I would assume that locking would be covered under altering or transmuting, so the chart would look more like<br /> <br /> To lock an effect to..................... Use<br /> <br /> A minor energy source................ Forces 3<br /> A major energy source................. Forces 5<br /> <br /> Simple life forms........................ Life 2<br /> Yourself...................................... Life 3<br /> Complex life forms.................... Life 4<br /> <br /> An simple inanimate object......... Matter 2 (i.e. homogeneous objects)<br /> A complex inanimate object ....... Matter 3 (i.e. heterogeneous objects)<br /> <br /> Spirit Ephemera.......................... Spirit 2<br /> Actual Spirits............................. Spirit 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 11-25-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:47:51-08:00","id":1008189,"title":"","content":"Ya I'd read locking as transmutation which fits your previous example well. Thing is life 2 forces 2 has been the typical invisibility rote forever. Including the magic effect chart in M20. Now all of a sudden HDYDT says rank 4. Now i agree with life 4 if its a permanent alteration. Which again fits the idea of a locked effect in a way I could agree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:53:03-08:00","id":1008194,"title":"","content":"Sorry for double post.<br /> <br /> The idea that really needs to be determined is whether there is a difference between &quot;linking&quot; an effect as with life 2 force 2 invisibility and &quot;locking&quot;, life 4 forces 2. <br /> <br /> If this is the definite case then I will start allowing locked effects whereas previously our group has stayed with the older ruling.<br /> <br /> Of course under this concept then locked effects would require a rank at which major pattern alteration could be accomplished. Which is 4 for most spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 11-25-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:28:38-08:00","id":1008251,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that you don't have to lock effects. It is nice but not the only way.<br /> Correspondence and Prime (Time sort of too) can be used to accomplish similar feats.<br /> <br /> I for one disregard the portion of locking effects that says: you don't suffer a malus of 1 per two effects if you locked these effects.<br /> Suddenly locking an effect is not nearly as important as before.<br /> <br /> Seriously if Life 3 is all you need to buff yourself with (relative) impunity then things get ridiculous even faster than before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:03:39-08:00","id":1008325,"title":"","content":"Locking in the Revised and earlier era required X: 2/3, per further up posts; in the M20 era, some targets are bumped to 3/4 (per HDYWTDT), which can be rationalized in some regards but in general is a more game-mechanic balancing factor than a metaphysically &quot;sound&quot; one (generally, 2 for most with 3 for some is the more metaphysically &quot;correct&quot; leveling). I suspect that when Mage is rejiggered again at some point in the future, the scaling will go back to 2/3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:21:39-08:00","id":1008330,"title":"","content":"And remember HDYDT even contradicts M20 on the invisibility rote. Which yes the M20 chart is basically a copy, paste from 2nd edition, but still it's there. Coupled with the fact that many people, myself included, pick and choose what to use from HDYDT I'd simply say to pick your method and stick to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:16:41-08:00","id":1008355,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone. As a long time gamer, it is really frustrating when source material contradicts itself, particularly in the first 2 books printed. Lack of internal consistency is one of my biggest pet peeves.<br /> <br /> That said, based as much on RAW as possible and as little house-ruling as possible, what people's preferred methods of creating sustained effects (combat buffs, armor, etc). Sphere ranks and successes needed would just as helpful as the core idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}